The allocation table leaves the pool, because bookkeeping may not live in memory that is given away.

Step two of putting this heap under Sublet, first half, and like step one it is meant to change
nothing: the table moves, nothing is carved and nothing is revoked yet. If the suite moves here,
it is the relayout and not the discipline.

WHY IT HAS TO MOVE. gc_setup_area carves the allocation table out of the front of the same block
it then allocates from. That is correct when the block is only memory. It is wrong when the block
is a region that gets carved into objects and given back, because a revocation cannot spare part
of what it covers, and the table is the one thing the collector must still be able to read after
a block dies. It is the metadata-layout class of the port recipe, the same rule that moves
memsys5's free-list links into aLink and PostgreSQL's into a side table.

WHAT IT SIMPLIFIES. Upstream solves for a table length such that table plus pool exactly fills the
block, which is the arithmetic in the #if MICROPY_ENABLE_FINALISER branch. With the table outside,
the pool IS the region and there is nothing to solve: blocks are (end - start) / BYTES_PER_BLOCK
and the table is one byte per four of them, plus the gap byte that has to read AT_FREE so the mark
phase cannot walk off the last block.

The port supplies the storage, as it supplies the handle slots, and carries the same invariant as
a file-scope assertion where both sizes are constants. gc_init asserts it too, because an
assertion is all it may do there: it runs before there is an NLR handler and a raise would hang
BOTH ARMS, NOT JUST THE PROTECTED ONE. The guard is MPY_HEAP_FROM_REGION and not MPY_SUBLET, and
the counters say why. Taking the table out of the pool makes the pool larger by the table's size,
and a larger pool collects less often: the same suite runs 54 cycles and collects 250,171 objects
with the table inside, and 53 and 250,593 with it outside. The program allocates exactly the same
either way, 369,904 times. If only the protected arm moved the table, it would be compared against
a collector that ran a different number of cycles, and every per-cycle number in the experiment
would carry that difference.

--- a/py/gc.h
+++ b/py/gc.h
@@ -137,4 +137,20 @@
 extern size_t mpy_gc_handles_len;
 #endif
 
+// MPY_HEAP_FROM_REGION: the pool arrives as a region and the allocation table therefore leaves it,
+// because bookkeeping may not live in memory the allocator hands away. This is NOT guarded by
+// MPY_SUBLET on purpose. Taking the table out of the pool makes the pool bigger by the table's
+// size, which changes when collections happen: with the table inside, the suite runs 54 cycles
+// and collects 250,171 objects; with it outside, 53 and 250,593. Both arms of the experiment have
+// to be on the same side of that, or the arm with the discipline would be compared against a
+// collector that ran a different number of times.
+#ifndef MPY_HEAP_FROM_REGION
+#define MPY_HEAP_FROM_REGION (0)
+#endif
+
+#if MPY_HEAP_FROM_REGION
+extern byte *mpy_gc_atb;
+extern size_t mpy_gc_atb_len;
+#endif
+
 #endif // MICROPY_INCLUDED_PY_GC_H
--- a/py/gc.c
+++ b/py/gc.c
@@ -159,6 +159,20 @@
     //     P = A * BLOCKS_PER_ATB * BYTES_PER_BLOCK
     // => T = A * (1 + BLOCKS_PER_ATB / BLOCKS_PER_FTB + BLOCKS_PER_ATB / BLOCKS_PER_WTB + BLOCKS_PER_ATB * BYTES_PER_BLOCK)
     size_t total_byte_len = (byte *)end - (byte *)start;
+    #if MPY_HEAP_FROM_REGION
+    // The region is pool and nothing else; the table is the port's. One byte of ATB covers
+    // BLOCKS_PER_ATB blocks, and the byte past the end has to read AT_FREE so that gc_mark_tree
+    // cannot walk off the last block, which is what ALLOC_TABLE_GAP_BYTE is for upstream.
+    size_t pool_blocks = total_byte_len / BYTES_PER_BLOCK;
+    area->gc_alloc_table_byte_len =
+        (pool_blocks + BLOCKS_PER_ATB - 1) / BLOCKS_PER_ATB;
+    assert(mpy_gc_atb_len >= area->gc_alloc_table_byte_len + ALLOC_TABLE_GAP_BYTE);
+    area->gc_alloc_table_start = mpy_gc_atb;
+    memset(mpy_gc_atb, 0, area->gc_alloc_table_byte_len + ALLOC_TABLE_GAP_BYTE);
+    area->gc_pool_start = (byte *)start;
+    area->gc_pool_end = (byte *)end;
+    size_t gc_pool_block_len = pool_blocks;
+    #else
     #if MICROPY_ENABLE_FINALISER || MICROPY_PY_WEAKREF
     area->gc_alloc_table_byte_len = (total_byte_len - ALLOC_TABLE_GAP_BYTE)
         * MP_BITS_PER_BYTE
@@ -197,8 +211,10 @@
     area->gc_pool_start = (byte *)end - gc_pool_block_len * BYTES_PER_BLOCK;
     area->gc_pool_end = end;
     assert(area->gc_pool_start >= next_table);
+    #endif  // MPY_HEAP_FROM_REGION
 
     // Clear ATB's, and FTB's and WTB's if they are enabled.
+    #if !MPY_HEAP_FROM_REGION
     memset(area->gc_alloc_table_start, 0,
         area->gc_alloc_table_byte_len + ALLOC_TABLE_GAP_BYTE
         #if MICROPY_ENABLE_FINALISER
@@ -208,6 +224,7 @@
         + gc_weakref_table_byte_len
         #endif
         );
+    #endif  // !MPY_HEAP_FROM_REGION
 
     area->gc_last_free_atb_index = 0;
     area->gc_last_used_block = 0;
